GAL16V8
ODTBRDGE

; SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
; Copyright (c) 2026 Dimitri Varpusvuori
; U6: DCJ11 bus controls for the DC319A DLART and startup buffer.
; Pin names starting with n describe active-low signals at the package.
; NOT TESTED ON REAL HARDWARE. See design.md for verification limits.

AIO3 AIO2 AIO1 AIO0 BS0 BS1 nSCTL nBUF ADDR0 GND
NC   nREAD PARK13 PARK14 nWRITE PARK16 PARK17 nSELECT nBOOT VCC

; The DLART occupies the external-I/O bank. A2:A0 select its registers.
/nSELECT = BS1 * /BS0

; Bus reads use AIO codes 8 through C. Drive data only while the CPU
; releases DAL. The DLART's chip-select input also qualifies this strobe.
/nREAD = /nBUF * AIO3 * /AIO2
        + /nBUF * AIO3 * /AIO1 * /AIO0

; Word and byte writes use codes 0 through 3. The DLART accepts its
; writable low byte at even addresses during the stretched phase.
/nWRITE = /AIO3 * /AIO2 * /ADDR0 * /nSCTL

; GP read (code E) selects the fixed startup word. U5 also checks nBUF.
/nBOOT = AIO3 * AIO2 * AIO1 * /AIO0

; Unconnected output pads have a defined state.
PARK13 = GND
PARK14 = GND
PARK16 = GND
PARK17 = GND

DESCRIPTION
ODT bridge for the DCJ11 test rig. See design.md for the specification
and proof. This source and the programming data it produces use the
MIT license in LICENSE.
